Don't fall into the trap of relying too much on the mattock. It is a
very strong weapon _now_, but it's two-handed. This means that it can't
be two-weaponed, so later on (with full enchantment) it will be worse
than Excalibur plus longsword (or if you have one, saber). There is
another downside to two-handed weapons which you won't need to worry
about until you get the Amulet.
Also, three keys and a lock pick is nice, but you only need one key.
They don't wear down. At most, keep a single spare in your bag in case
your main one get stolen.

